          "id": "12321837",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl",
            "name": "paul.elschot@xs4all.nl",
            "key": "paul.elschot@xs4all.nl",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180"
            },
            "displayName": "Paul Elschot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "The first attachment actually is InputStream.java, in the store package. \n \nI left in some comments and commented code. The initial buffer size \nand the buffer size increase factor might need tweaking. It passes \nall the current tests, and the commented println's confirm the working. \n \nI have not tested this on larger indexes with a lot of of query activity. \n \nRegards, \nPaul \n ",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl",
            "name": "paul.elschot@xs4all.nl",
            "key": "paul.elschot@xs4all.nl",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180"
            },
            "displayName": "Paul Elschot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2004-08-16T04:04:19.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-08-16T04:04:19.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12314414/comment/12321838",
          "id": "12321838",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl",
            "name": "paul.elschot@xs4all.nl",
            "key": "paul.elschot@xs4all.nl",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=paul.elschot%40xs4all.nl&avatarId=23180"
            },
            "displayName": "Paul Elschot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Possible flaw in the attached java file: clone() evt. truncates \nthe buffer, but in that case it does not reseek the underlying \nstream to the new end of the buffer. \n ",
          "updateAuthor": {
